// CoRR -- one thread writes 1 then 2, another reads 2 and then 1. Non-atomic
// reads need not be coherent in OCaml: a read does not advance the thread's
// frontier, so the second may read an older write. SC forbids it.
//
// The OCaml memory model (Dolan, Sivaramakrishnan & Madhavapeddy, PLDI 2018,
// section 6). An access in mode sc is to an atomic location, any other access
// non-atomic.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  x := 2
} ||| {
  r1 := x;
  r2 := x
}
%%
allow (r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [OCaml]
forbid (r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [SC]
